5. The 0.4 benchmark's pictures

   Fifteen pictures: twelve museum works and three made with an image
   generator. bench/PICTURES.md has the same credits as a table. Each
   citation reads: artist, title, date; medium; size; museum (accession
   number) and its credit line; rights; link. The words are the museum's
   own record, read on 23 November 2026. Most of the full-size files are
   held outside this repository; the files that are in it are named in
   sections 1, 2 and 4. Paintings of these pictures made by the painter
   follow section 3 (museum works) or section 1 (Mittens and Kasha).

   Rights. Art Institute of Chicago: the record marks the work public
   domain, and the museum releases such images under CC0
   (https://www.artic.edu/open-access/open-access-images). Cleveland: the
   record's licence is CC0. The Met: the record marks the work public
   domain, and Open Access images are CC0 (section 2); where our file is
   the Met's own file as donated to Wikimedia Commons, the Commons page
   follows.

